{
  "schema": "semio.editor.text-input/v1",
  "provenance": {
    "what": "The text-input model of the canvas text editor (EditorHost + the TextEditor host): typing inserts at the caret or replaces the exact selection, Backspace/Delete remove one character or the exact selection, arrows move one character (a selection collapses to its edge), Home/End go to the line edges, a paste or an IME composition commits its text like typing it. Semantic tokens never move an edit and no space is ever implied.",
    "sequences": "Each sequence starts from `text` with the selection `[anchor, caret]` (offsets in Unicode scalar values — every implementation converts to its own units), applies `steps` in order and must end at `expect`. `type` presses one key per character; `key` presses one named key; `select` sets the selection; `paste` and `compose` commit a whole string at once. Every sequence runs under BOTH schedules of the `tokenizer`: `fast` keeps the initial tokens for the whole sequence (the guest's tokens never arrive in between), `slow` re-tokenizes the current text after every step (they always do). The answer must not depend on the schedule.",
    "tokenizer": "word-runs: every maximal run of ASCII letters, digits and `_` is one semantic token of class `ident`.",
    "echoes": "The host's optimistic local echo: the host keeps the texts it sent as edits and not yet seen echoed (`local`) and the last text an echo acknowledged. A scene buffer equal to a pending text acknowledges it and every older one — its buffer and selection are applied only when it is the NEWEST pending edit (an older one would revert typing that is still in flight); a buffer equal to the last acknowledged text while edits are still pending is the guest re-publishing a state it already echoed (a job finishing) and is not applied either; any other buffer is an external change (undo, a collaborator, a formatter) and is applied at once, dropping every pending edit. `expect` is the host's text after the event, `pending` the edits still in flight.",
    "oracles": [
      "Chromium's native <textarea> editing, driven with real key events by Playwright (the `sequences`, monospace font; `paste`/`compose` via insertText)",
      "🧰️framework/🔨️modules/✍️editor/🦀️.rs — EditorHost (Rust law, both schedules)",
      "🧰️framework/🛍️products/💻️os/🔨️modules/📺️renderer/🧑‍🎨engine/🧱️elements/✏️TextEditor/🟦️.tsx — reconcileTextEditorEchoV1 (the `echoes`)"
    ]
  },
